{"id": "EUVD-2026-108912", "enisaUuid": "517c9b9e-ffb2-3408-815a-452119572237", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: qcom: lpass-cpu: use DAI table index for playback constraints\n\nThe DAI ID is a hardware port ID and is not necessarily the index of\nthe corresponding entry in variant->dai_driver.\n\nWhen configuring a DAI with LPAIF_I2SCTL_MODE_QUAD01, the probe code\ncurrently uses dai_id to index variant->dai_driver. This is incorrect\nfor platforms where DAI IDs are sparse. For example, the IPQ806x MI2S\nDAI has ID 4 while it is the only entry in the DAI driver table. If\nthat DAI is configured for QUAD01 and probe reaches this branch, the\ncode writes beyond that single entry via dai_driver[4] instead of\nupdating the DAI being processed.\n\nUse the loop index i when updating the current DAI's playback channel\nconstraints, while retaining dai_id for indexing the hardware-port\nspecific playback SD-line mode array.\n\nThis fixes the incorrect DAI table access for platforms where the DAI\nID does not match its position in the driver table.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:12:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:12:08", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/775df6a27e8433e2414124472938009b958f9a77", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6833f1893ac2ec40016c348779af63debf3700d2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/69d2b7a4c115181629eb14d800aecc3e7de3f7fb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f11336e6d3cd9e28e5cdf1cb8a6171e7c3eff4e4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ca51771c8efde5df05476ac98dd1b2af4e2b149f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98940"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "25d9513a-9dbe-3bda-aadd-17d5c34ffe52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "33347a14-7be0-3d9c-8f0e-6fa80b9e84b6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4dabf261-e424-3e74-99b2-507326cba170", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c223f41c1a52bfe10f1d3311679b1d1f9813e500 <f11336e6d3cd9e28e5cdf1cb8a6171e7c3eff4e4"}, {"id": "574b33d9-10f5-34d3-a702-5556c883b8b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.14"}, {"id": "8d576b92-5a6c-3d23-a10f-0b6b7e86544e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "94fbe5de-ff2f-35cb-8c85-b771512c6bfc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c223f41c1a52bfe10f1d3311679b1d1f9813e500 <69d2b7a4c115181629eb14d800aecc3e7de3f7fb"}, {"id": "9971005f-6609-3892-94ca-bb42d2817d4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "b9e4e74b-ab23-3ba8-add2-e355c0ad97e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "d8e592f9-d579-3b74-9497-d22b7803fa7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c223f41c1a52bfe10f1d3311679b1d1f9813e500 <ca51771c8efde5df05476ac98dd1b2af4e2b149f"}, {"id": "e8b539a1-6c54-3a8e-be87-0f1b4718c2cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c223f41c1a52bfe10f1d3311679b1d1f9813e500 <775df6a27e8433e2414124472938009b958f9a77"}, {"id": "ef57ebd3-2161-357f-aeca-0aaa55881546", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c223f41c1a52bfe10f1d3311679b1d1f9813e500 <6833f1893ac2ec40016c348779af63debf3700d2"}, {"id": "f664f47c-58c6-35b9-aeeb-d013f47d1f81", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0be28ef2-b69a-3380-b0a2-0b9b50c59e07", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}